arks/", "https://github.com/universal-commerce-protocol/ucp", "https://github.com/universal-commerce-protocol", "https://ucp.dev/documentation/core-concepts/"], "checked_at": "2026-10-02", "notes": "Announced 2026-01-11 at NRF as built with Shopify, Etsy, Wayfair, Target and Walmart and endorsed by 20+ more. Latest GitHub release seen: v2026-04-08 (2026-04-09); search results show a 2026-08-25 spec path on ucp.dev that was not fetched. Payment is delegated to pluggable 'payment handlers' (examples: com.google.pay, dev.shopify.shop_pay) and supports AP2 mandates, hence money='any'; ucp.dev home page could not be fetched directly."}, {"name": "MCP", "full_name": "Model Context Protocol", "role": "tool_access", "one_liner": "A standard plug that lets AI assistants connect to outside tools and data; payment protocols are often delivered through it.", "best_for": "Connecting agents to tools, data and paid services", "money": ["none"], "stewards": ["Agentic AI Foundation (Linux Foundation)", "Anthropic (original author)"], "governance": "Donated by Anthropic to the Agentic AI Foundation, a Linux Foundation directed fund co-founded by Anthropic, Block and OpenAI (2025-12-09); decisions remain with maintainers via the SEP process", "status": "production", "launched": "2024-11", "official_url": "https://modelcontextprotocol.io", "spec_url": "https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/changelog", "github_repo": "modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol", "networks": [], "sources": ["https://blog.modelcontextprotocol.io/posts/2025-12-09-mcp-joins-agentic-ai-foundation/", "https://blog.modelcontextprotocol.io/posts/2026-07-28/", "https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/releases", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Model_Context_Protocol"], "checked_at": "2026-10-02", "notes": "Latest stable spec revision is 2026-07-28 (stateless protocol core, no initialize handshake). Initial release date (2024-11-25) comes from Wikipedia, not a primary source. MCP has no payment function itself; x402 Bazaar, MPP and Agentic.Market expose MCP servers. spec_url appeared in search results and was not fetched."}, {"name": "A2A", "full_name": "Agent2Agent Protocol", "role": "agent_communication", "one_liner": "A shared language that lets AI agents from different companies find each other, talk and hand over tasks.", "best_for": "Agent-to-agent task delegation and collaboration", "money": ["none"], "stewards": ["Linux Foundation (A2A project)", "Google (original author)"], "governance": "Linux Foundation project since 2025-06-23; Technical Steering Committee with AWS, Cisco, Google, IBM Research, Microsoft, Salesforce, SAP and ServiceNow; Apache 2.0", "status": "spec_published", "launched": "2025-04", "official_url": "https://a2a-protocol.org/latest/", "spec_url": "https://a2a-protocol.org/latest/specification/", "github_repo": "a2aproject/A2A", "networks": [], "sources": ["https://a2a-protocol.org/latest/", "https://a2a-protocol.org/latest/specification/", "https://github.com/a2aproject/A2A", "https://www.linuxfoundation.org/press/linux-foundation-launches-the-agent2agent-protocol-project-to-enable-secure-intelligent-communication-between-ai-agents", "https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/ai-machine-learning/announcing-agents-to-payments-ap2-protocol"], "checked_at": "2026-10-02", "notes": "Latest released spec version shown is 1.0.0 (release date not verified). No native payments; Google's AP2 announcement describes an 'A2A x402 extension' for crypto payments, and AP2/UCP build on A2A."}, {"name": "Visa TAP", "full_name": "Visa Trusted Agent Protocol (part of Visa Intelligent Commerce)", "role": "card_network_framework", "one_liner": "Lets online shops check that an AI shopping agent is genuine and approved by Visa, rather than a malicious bot.", "best_for": "Merchants recognising trusted agents at card checkout", "money": ["card"], "stewards": ["Visa"], "governance": "Visa-published framework developed with Cloudflare; built on HTTP Message Signatures (RFC 9421) / Web Bot Auth; Visa states an aim to align with IETF, OpenID Foundation and EMVCo", "status": "spec_published", "launched": "2025-10", "official_url": "https://developer.visa.com/capabilities/trusted-agent-protocol/overview", "spec_url": "https://developer.visa.com/capabilities/trusted-agent-protocol/overview", "github_repo": "visa/trusted-agent-protocol", "networks": [], "sources": ["https://developer.visa.com/capabilities/trusted-agent-protocol/overview", "https://github.com/visa/trusted-agent-protocol", "https://investor.visa.com/news/news-details/2025/Visa-Introduces-Trusted-Agent-Protocol-An-Ecosystem-Led-Framework-for-AI-Commerce/default.aspx", "https://usa.visa.com/about-visa/newsroom/press-releases.releaseId.21361.html", "https://corporate.visa.com/en/sites/visa-perspectives/newsroom/visa-intelligent-commerce-connect-ai-shopping-for-businesses.html"], "checked_at": "2026-10-02", "notes": "TAP announced 2025-10-14; the parent programme Visa Intelligent Commerce was announced 2025-04-30. Visa's developer page still says the product 'is in the process of development and deployment'. Visa Intelligent Commerce Connect (2026-04-08, in pilot) accepts TAP, MPP, ACP and UCP. GitHub repo is a sample implementation; licence not verified."}, {"name": "Mastercard Agent Pay", "full_name": "Mastercard Agent Pay (Agentic Tokens / Agent Pay Acceptance Framework)", "role": "card_network_framework", "one_liner": "Mastercard's programme that gives AI agents special secure card tokens so they can pay on a cardholder's behalf with consent.", "best_for": "Card payments made by AI agents on Mastercard", "money": ["card"], "stewards": ["Mastercard"], "governance": "Proprietary Mastercard programme; Agent Pay Acceptance Framework shared on Mastercard Developers for industry feedback; uses Web Bot Auth for agent verification", "status": "production", "launched": "2025-04", "official_url": "https://investor.mastercard.com/investor-news/investor-news-details/2025/Mastercard-Unveils-Agent-Pay-Pioneering-Agentic-Payments-Technology-to-Power-Commerce-in-the-Age-of-AI/default.aspx", "spec_url": null, "github_repo": null, "networks": [], "sources": ["https://investor.mastercard.com/investor-news/investor-news-details/2025/Mastercard-Unveils-Agent-Pay-Pioneering-Agentic-Payments-Technology-to-Power-Commerce-in-the-Age-of-AI/default.aspx", "https://www.mastercard.com/us/en/news-and-trends/stories/2025/agentic-commerce-framework.html", "https://www.mastercard.com/global/en/news-and-trends/stories/2025/agentic-commerce-momentum.html", "https://www.mastercard.com/us/en/news-and-trends/press/2025/september/mastercard-unveils-new-tools-and-collaborations-to-power-smarter,-safer-agentic-commerce.html"], "checked_at": "2026-10-02", "notes": "Announced 2025-04-29. Mastercard said Citi and U.S. Bank cardholders were already enabled and that all U.S. cardholders would be enabled by mid-November 2025 with global rollout to follow; completion of that rollout was not verified. The Mastercard product page and developer docs could not be fetched, so official_url is the launch press release and spec_url is null."}, {"name": "Verifiable Intent", "full_name": "Verifiable Intent", "role": "authorization", "one_liner": "Creates a tamper-resistant record of what a person authorised an AI agent to do, as cryptographic proof if a purchase is disputed.", "best_for": "Proof of user authorisation for agent purchases, dispute evidence", "money": [], "stewards": ["Mastercard", "Google"], "governance": "Open-sourced by Mastercard (co-developed with Google); built on FIDO Alliance, EMVCo, IETF and W3C specifications; aligned with AP2 and UCP; no standards-body ownership verified", "status": "spec_published", "launched": "2026-03", "official_url": "https://verifiableintent.dev/", "spec_url": null, "github_repo": "agent-intent/verifiable-intent", "networks": [], "sources": ["https://www.mastercard.com/us/en/news-and-trends/stories/2026/verifiable-intent.html", "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/platforms/google-pay/agent-payments-protocol-fido-alliance/"], "checked_at": "2026-10-02", "notes": "Announced 2026-03-05; Mastercard said it would be integrated into Agent Pay's intent APIs. The website and GitHub repo URLs come from the Mastercard article and were not fetched themselves; payment rails are not specified, so money is left empty."}, {"name": "KYAPay", "full_name": "KYAPay (Know Your Agent + Pay) protocol", "role": "identity", "one_liner": "Gives an AI agent a verifiable ID card and a payment token, so a service knows who the agent represents and can charge it.", "best_for": "Agent identity verification, account creation and guest checkout", "money": ["card", "stablecoin", "bank_transfer"], "stewards": ["Skyfire"], "governance": "Open spec under Community Specification License 1.0 in Skyfire's GitHub; working group formation pending; token format submitted as individual IETF Internet-Draft draft-skyfire-oauth-kyapay-token (not endorsed by IETF)", "status": "draft", "launched": "2025-06", "official_url": "https://kyapay.org", "spec_url": "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-skyfire-oauth-kyapay-token-00", "github_repo": "skyfire-xyz/kyapay", "networks": [], "sources": ["https://github.com/skyfire-xyz/kyapay", "https://kyapay.org", "https://kyapay.org/whitepaper", "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-skyfire-oauth-kyapay-token-00", "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250626772489/en/Skyfire-Launches-Open-KYAPay-Protocol-With-Agent-Checkout"], "checked_at": "2026-10-02", "notes": "Launched 2025-06-26 with three JWT token types (KYA, Pay, KYA+Pay); buyer wallets funded by card, USDC or ACH. The GitHub README says full specification v1.0 is 'aimed to be released soon'. Datatracker shows newer draft versions (-01, -02) than the -00 fetched; exact dates of those versions not verified."}, {"name": "L402", "full_name": "L402 (Lightning HTTP 402 Protocol, formerly LSAT)", "role": "pay_per_request", "one_liner": "Lets software pay a tiny Bitcoin Lightning invoice to unlock an API, and the payment receipt doubles as the login.", "best_for": "Bitcoin micro-payments for APIs, no accounts", "money": ["lightning"], "stewards": ["Lightning Labs"], "governance": "Open specification published by Lightning Labs on GitHub (MIT licence); no standards body", "status": "production", "launched": "2020-03", "official_url": "https://l402.tech/", "spec_url": "https://docs.lightning.engineering/the-lightning-network/l402/protocol-specification", "github_repo": "lightninglabs/L402", "networks": ["Bitcoin Lightning Network"], "sources": ["https://github.com/lightninglabs/L402", "https://docs.lightning.engineering/the-lightning-network/l402", "https://docs.lightning.engineering/the-lightning-network/l402/protocol-specification", "https://lightning.engineering/posts/2020-03-30-lsat/", "https://l402.tech/"], "checked_at": "2026-10-02", "notes": "First published 2020-03-30 as LSAT (Lightning Service Authentication Tokens); the original post is now titled L402. The date of the rename was not verified. Lightning Labs states it runs in production across Lightning Loop, Pool and Aperture; the repo now includes an 'Agent Specification'."}, {"name": "Web Bot Auth", "full_name": "Web Bot Auth (HTTP Message Signatures for automated traffic)", "role": "identity", "one_liner": "Lets bots and AI agents cryptographically sign their web requests so websites can verify who they really are.", "best_for": "Verifying bot/agent identity at the CDN or website edge", "money": ["none"], "stewards": ["IETF Web Bot Auth Working Group", "Cloudflare (draft author)"], "governance": "Active IETF working group (webbotauth), charter approved; builds on RFC 9421; base draft draft-meunier-web-bot-auth-architecture authored at Cloudflare; not yet an RFC", "status": "draft", "launched": "2025", "official_url": "https://datatracker.ietf.org/wg/webbotauth/about/", "spec_url": "https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-meunier-web-bot-auth-architecture-02.html", "github_repo": null, "networks": [], "sources": ["https://datatracker.ietf.org/wg/webbotauth/about/", "https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-meunier-web-bot-auth-architecture-02.html", "https://blog.cloudflare.com/verified-bots-with-cryptography/", "https://www.webbotauth.org/"], "checked_at": "2026-10-02", "notes": "Not a payment protocol but the identity layer under Visa TAP, Mastercard Agent Pay and Cloudflare pay per crawl. The WG charter puts HTTP APIs and agent-to-agent interfaces out of scope. WG milestones (standards-track specs April 2026, BCP August 2026) were listed; whether they were met was not verified. webbotauth.org is an independent directory, not an official site."}, {"name": "Pay per crawl", "full_name": "Cloudflare Pay Per Crawl", "role": "pay_per_request", "one_liner": "Lets website owners charge AI crawlers a price each time they fetch a page, with Cloudflare handling the billing.", "best_for": "Publishers charging AI crawlers for content access", "money": [], "stewards": ["Cloudflare"], "governance": "Proprietary Cloudflare feature (not an open standard); Cloudflare acts as Merchant of Record", "status": "draft", "launched": "2025-07", "official_url": "https://blog.cloudflare.com/introducing-pay-per-crawl/", "spec_url": "https://developers.cloudflare.com/ai-crawl-control/features/pay-per-crawl/use-pay-per-crawl-as-ai-owner/crawl-pages/", "github_repo": null, "networks": [], "sources": ["https://blog.cloudflare.com/introducing-pay-per-crawl/", "https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2025-07-01-pay-per-crawl/", "https://developers.cloudflare.com/ai-crawl-control/features/pay-per-crawl/use-pay-per-crawl-as-ai-owner/crawl-pages/", "https://blog.cloudflare.com/x402/"], "checked_at": "2026-10-02", "notes": "Launched 2025-07-01 in private beta; current docs do not say whether it is still beta, so status 'draft' means beta/unverified GA. Uses HTTP 402 with crawler-price / crawler-exact-price / crawler-max-price / crawler-charged headers and requires Web Bot Auth signatures. Charges go to the crawler's Cloudflare account (changelog mentions Stripe for site owners); exact rails not documented, so money is empty. Cloudflare said an x402 'deferred' scheme would be integrated."}]$pay$::jsonb, $pay$[{"name": "Stripe", "company": "Stripe, Inc.", "website": "https://stripe.com", "kind": "payment_processor", "one_liner": "Payment processor that lets agents pay by card (Shared Payment Tokens) or stablecoin over MPP and x402, settling to a Stripe balance.", "agentic_product": "Agentic Commerce Suite / Machine payments (Shared Payment Tokens, Link Agent Wallet)", "protocols": ["MPP", "x402", "ACP", "UCP"], "protocol_sources": {"MPP": "https://docs.stripe.com/payments/machine", "x402": "https://docs.stripe.com/payments/machine", "ACP": "https://docs.stripe.com/agentic-commerce", "UCP": "https://docs.stripe.com/agentic-commerce"}, "rails": ["card", "stablecoin", "bank_transfer", "wallet"], "networks": ["Tempo", "Solana", "Base", "Ethereum", "Polygon"], "fees": [{"label": "Online card (US, domestic)", "percent": 2.9, "fixed": 0.3, "currency": "USD", "description": "2.9% + 30¢ per successful transaction for domestic cards", "region": "US"}, {"label": "International cards surcharge", "percent": 1.5, "fixed": null, "currency": "USD", "description": "+1.5% for international cards", "region": "US"}, {"label": "Currency conversion", "percent": 1.0, "fixed": null, "currency": "USD", "description": "+1% if currency conversion is required", "region": "US"}, {"label": "Stablecoin payments", "percent": 1.5, "fixed": null, "currency": "USD", "description": "1.5% of the transaction amount in USD", "region": "US"}, {"label": "ACH Direct Debit", "percent": 0.8, "fixed": null, "currency": "USD", "description": "0.8% ACH Direct Debit, $5.00 cap", "region": "US"}, {"label": "Agentic commerce: Shared Payment Token", "percent": null, "fixed": 0.15, "currency": "USD", "description": "$0.15 per SPT issued", "region": "US"}], "pricing_public": true, "pricing_url": "https://stripe.com/pricing", "pricing_verified": true, "kyc_required": null, "regions": "SPTs: all US states (other countries listed in docs). Stablecoin machine payments: all US states except New York; 30+ other countries on request.", "sources": ["https://stripe.com/pricing", "https://docs.stripe.com/payments/machine", "https://docs.stripe.com/payments/machine/mpp", "https://docs.stripe.com/agentic-commerce", "https://docs.stripe.com/payments/stablecoin-payments", "https://stripe.com/newsroom/news/agentic-commerce-suite"], "checked_at": "2026-10-02", "notes": "US pricing page only; fees differ by country. Machine-payment minimums: 0.50 USD by card (SPT), 0.01 USDC by stablecoin. x402 on Stripe = USDC on Base; MPP = USDC.e on Tempo and USDC on Solana. The SPT fee line was read via a page summary; re-check wording before publishing."}, {"name": "Coinbase Developer Platform", "company": "Coinbase, Inc.", "website": "https://www.coinbase.com/developer-platform", "kind": "x402_facilitator", "one_liner": "Runs the CDP x402 facilitator plus agent wallets (Agentic Wallets, Payments MCP) for stablecoin payments by AI agents.", "agentic_product": "x402 Facilitator / Agentic Wallets / Payments MCP / Coinbase for Agents", "protocols": ["x402", "MCP"], "protocol_sources": {"x402": "https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/x402/core-concepts/facilitator", "MCP": "https://www.coinbase.com/developer-platform/discover/launches/payments-mcp"}, "rails": ["stablecoin", "wallet"], "networks": ["Base", "Polygon", "Arbitrum", "World", "Solana"], "fees": [{"label": "x402 facilitator: free tier", "percent": null, "fixed": 0, "currency": "USD", "description": "Up to 1,000 transactions per month free", "region": "global"}, {"label": "x402 facilitator: per transaction", "percent": null, "fixed": 0.001, "currency": "USD", "description": "$0.001 per transaction beyond the free tier", "region": "global"}], "pricing_publi